<title>JAPAN: Japan 1997/98 magnesium demand seen up 5.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Japan 1997/98 magnesium demand seen up 5.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese magnesium demand is expected to rise 5.5 percent to 30,720 tonnes in the current fiscal year which started on April 1, the Japan Magnesium Association said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Figures for Japanese magnesium demand were as follows:</p>
<p>(in tonnes with year-on-year percentage change)</p>
<p>		     1997/98	1996/97     year/year change</p>
<p> Castings	   3,300	  2,450	   +34.7 pct</p>
<p> Aluminium	 22,200	 21,850	    +1.6 pct</p>
<p> Other		3,200	  2,700	   +18.5 pct</p>
<p> Domestic total  30,650	 29,040	    +5.5 pct</p>
<p> Exports		 70	     70	    unchanged</p>
<p> TOTAL	     30,720	 29,110	    +5.5 pct</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
